      "writtenOn": "2026-05-08T18:26:20Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "**Mixing `std::print` and `std::cout`**\n\n* **Issue:** `setProgressBar` mixes `logInfo` (which wraps `std::print`) and `std::cout \u003c\u003c std::flush;`. These use different underlying I/O mechanisms (`stdout` vs iostreams) and can lead to interleaved or poorly synchronized terminal output.  \n* **Remediation:** Stick to one. When using `std::print`, force a flush by using `std::fflush(stdout);`.",
      "range": {
